# `into[i] = value`, `into` the answer of a call that nobody sees: nothing is expected of it. The loop's own text says that it is stored into under a counter and that nothing is named off it:
# it is asked in front of the loop for a list, for bytes, for doubles and for floats, and each has a copy of the loop with a store of its own. What is none of them runs the loop as it was.
# RUN(ANYTHING): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# ANYTHING-LABEL: code f1:Body
# ANYTHING: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Array #
# ANYTHING: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Buffer|Uint8Array #
# ANYTHING: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Float64Array #
# ANYTHING: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Float32Array #
# ANYTHING: = PutArrayElement
# ANYTHING: = PutTypedArrayElement {{*}} typedArrayType=2
# ANYTHING: = PutTypedArrayElement {{*}} typedArrayType=10
# ANYTHING: = PutTypedArrayElement {{*}} typedArrayType=9
# ANYTHING: = ElemSet
# A written whole number holds no fraction: doubles and floats stand among the other views, whose kind the store reads off the cell.
# RUN(WHOLE): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# WHOLE-LABEL: code f2:Body
